---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<html lang="en" class="dark">
  <head>
    <BaseHead 
      title="Privacy & Cookie Policy" 
      description="Privacy policy, data protection, and Google AdSense cookie disclosure for AutoCyberLab." 
      lang="en"
      translationSlug="privacidad"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-[#0A0D12] text-neutral-200 min-h-screen flex flex-col font-sans">
    <Header lang="en" alternateUrl="/es/privacidad/" />

    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-14 flex-grow w-full">
      <div class="mb-10 border-b border-neutral-800 pb-8">
        <span class="bg-[#00D36C] text-black text-xs font-black font-mono uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1">
          LEGAL DISCLOSURE // GDPR & CCPA
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mt-4 mb-2">
          Privacy & Cookie Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase">Last updated: October 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-base">
        <p>
          At <strong>AutoCyberLab</strong> (accessible from <code>https://autocyberlab.com</code>), one of our main priorities is the privacy of our visitors. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information that is collected and recorded by AutoCyberLab and how we use it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white border-l-4 border-[#00D36C] pl-3 mt-8">1. Log Files</h2>
        <p>
          AutoCyberLab follows a standard procedure of using log files. These files log visitors when they visit websites. The information collected by log files includes internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date and time stamp, referring/exit pages, and possibly the number of clicks. These are not linked to any information that is personally identifiable. The purpose of the information is for analyzing trends, administering the site, and ensuring network security.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white border-l-4 border-[#00D36C] pl-3 mt-8">2. Google AdSense & DoubleClick DART Cookie</h2>
        <p>
          Google is a third-party vendor on our site. It also uses cookies, known as DART cookies, to serve ads to our site visitors based upon their visit to <code>autocyberlab.com</code> and other sites on the internet.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-neutral-300">
          <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
          <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our users based on their visit to our sites and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
          <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#00D36C] underline">Google Ads Settings</a> or by visiting the Google ad and content network Privacy Policy at <code>https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads</code>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white border-l-4 border-[#00D36C] pl-3 mt-8">3. GDPR & CCPA Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>
          If you are visiting from the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or California (CCPA), you have the right to request access to, rectification of, or erasure of your personal data, as well as the right to manage your cookie consent preferences at any time via our consent management banner.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white border-l-4 border-[#00D36C] pl-3 mt-8">4. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          If you have additional questions or require more information about our Privacy Policy, please contact us through our <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-[#00D36C] underline">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>